Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.04,0:00:03.79,Main - Italics,KYLE/NA,0,0,0,,There are humanoid species,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.79,0:00:09.40,Main - Italics,KYLE/NA,0,0,0,,such as humans, elves, and dwarves,\Nwho are blessed by the gods of light.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.98,0:00:14.42,Main - Italics,KYLE/NA,0,0,0,,Then there are demons, \Nwhich, while few in number,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.42,0:00:17.67,Main - Italics,KYLE/NA,0,0,0,,are blessed by darkness and individually\Nfar stronger than humanoids.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.44,0:00:22.81,Main - Italics,KYLE/NA,0,0,0,,These two forces have clashed for millennia,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.81,0:00:25.53,Main - Italics,KYLE/NA,0,0,0,,dividing the vast continent of Leunders\N into the east and west.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.50,0:00:32.28,Main - Italics,KYLE/NA,0,0,0,,However, when a moderate demon king\N took the throne three hundred years ago,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.71,0:00:36.01,Main - Italics,KYLE/NA,0,0,0,,the situation stabilized, and humanoids \Ngrew accustomed to a temporary peace.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.76,0:00:40.60,Main - Italics,KYLE/NA,0,0,0,,In the fifth month of the year 2826,\N that peace was broken,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.00,0:00:45.31,Main - Italics,KYLE/NA,0,0,0,,and under a new demon king, \Nthe demons launched an all-out attack
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.63,0:00:50.28,Main - Italics,KYLE/NA,0,0,0,,against the humanoids that would\N be known as the Great Invasion.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.58,0:00:55.96,Main - Italics,KYLE/NA,0,0,0,,With no regard for their own casualties, \Nthe demons fought fiercely,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.96,0:00:59.94,Main - Italics,KYLE/NA,0,0,0,,and several humanoid nations\N fell the blink of an eye.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.70,0:01:04.67,Main - Italics,KYLE/NA,0,0,0,,By the fourth month \Nof the following year, 2827,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.13,0:01:09.67,Main - Italics,KYLE/NA,0,0,0,,the Gargan Empire, which boasted the largest\Nhumanoid fighting force, was destroyed.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.67,0:01:15.35,Main - Italics,KYLE/NA,0,0,0,,With nowhere left to turn, \Nhumanoids took desperate measures.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.18,0:01:18.40,Main - Italics,KYLE/NA,0,0,0,,They gathered their remaining troops
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.40,0:01:21.84,Main - Italics,KYLE/NA,0,0,0,,and engaged the main \Ndemon army in a reckless battle
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.84,0:01:26.81,Main - Italics,KYLE/NA,0,0,0,,while a suicide squad entered the demon king's\N castle, functionally the enemy base,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.81,0:01:30.44,Main - Italics,KYLE/NA,0,0,0,,to assassinate the demon king \Nin a final act of desperation.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.87,0:02:07.64,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Are you all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.30,0:02:23.20,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Theron!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.20,0:02:24.91,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,Go on without me.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.55,0:02:27.71,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,I'll handle these guys.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.99,0:02:31.21,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,We're counting on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.83,0:02:45.60,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,Damn... What a pain in the ass.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.63,0:03:03.70,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.61,0:03:16.51,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,What is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.71,0:03:20.09,Default,SILDONIA,0,0,0,,Above you!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.65,0:03:37.78,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Urza!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.03,0:04:35.35,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,What was that attack?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.71,0:04:41.67,Default,SILDONIA,0,0,0,,That was Elimination, an unblockable \Nhigh-level spell that destroys everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.60,0:04:44.97,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,I need to do something drastic.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.19,0:04:49.43,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,My only option is to release \Nthe gemstone's magic power.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.82,0:04:54.52,Default,SILDONIA,0,0,0,,If my wielder is risking his life, \Nthen I have no choice but to join you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.50,0:04:56.64,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.60,0:05:04.91,Default,SILDONIA,0,0,0,,Laws of wisdom, become a flash of light \Nto destroy the ignorance of darkness!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.69,0:05:53.86,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,It's finally over.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.19,0:05:55.87,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Hey.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.42,0:05:59.57,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,You can't respond to me anymore, can you?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.83,0:06:09.23,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,It's quiet.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.09,0:06:12.24,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,I guess I'm the only survivor.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.11,0:06:19.66,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,Everything I wanted to protect is gone now.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.17,0:06:25.75,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,My home, my family, my friends, my beloved...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.75,0:06:27.90,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,I've lost them all.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.10,0:06:36.28,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,Now, at last, I too can...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.65,0:06:55.96,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,A magical item?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.59,0:06:58.77,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,If that thing's magic power \Ngoes out of control...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.09,0:08:16.39,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Is this... my room?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.59,0:08:21.27,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,No, that's impossible.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.88,0:08:41.78,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,I must be dreaming.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.08,0:08:46.60,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,Kyle, how long are you going to sleep?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.60,0:08:48.31,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,Get up already.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.19,0:08:53.51,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,Oh, you're already awake.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.62,0:08:56.01,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Liese...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.64,0:08:58.26,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,Hey.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.15,0:09:02.14,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,What's wrong? Does your stomach hurt?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.90,0:09:07.52,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.47,0:09:12.45,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,I get it now. This is a dream.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.66,0:09:19.95,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,W-Wait a minute...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.95,0:09:21.51,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,I don't care if it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.82,0:09:23.91,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,I'm so glad to see you again, Liese.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.91,0:09:25.88,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,What's gotten into you?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.57,0:09:55.85,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,What are you thinking?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.85,0:10:00.03,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,I don't know what that was, but I need \Ntime to emotionally prepare myself!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.09,0:10:03.54,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,You jerk!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.94,0:10:09.88,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.74,0:10:11.83,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,I can feel pain.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.19,0:10:14.15,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Maybe it's not a dream?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.00,0:10:26.96,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,Yeah, it's not a dream.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.12,0:10:39.67,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,I'm younger, aren't I?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.57,0:10:43.99,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,Moreover, I thought I suffered \Nnear-fatal injuries.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.43,0:10:47.82,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,If this isn't a dream, what's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.90,0:11:03.82,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,The town is back to normal.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.82,0:11:06.16,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,Liese is alive and well, and I'm young again.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.86,0:11:09.10,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,I can only assume I've returned to the past.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.01,0:11:17.92,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,But that's not possible. \NDoes that mean this thing was the cause?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.33,0:11:22.53,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,There's no way a spell to return to the past—
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.78,0:11:27.50,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,Whatever the case, \NI guess I still get hungry.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.51,0:11:34.57,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,Liese must've made this for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.55,0:11:41.55,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,She frequently came over to cook, \Nsince my mom and I couldn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.18,0:11:48.41,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,That's good!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.80,0:11:51.90,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,I haven't had a proper meal in so long.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.77,0:12:03.95,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,I ate way too much.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.00,0:12:07.90,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,Hey. I'm starving.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.93,0:12:10.31,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,What? Hang on!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.67,0:12:14.67,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,You've gotta be kidding me!\NYou ate it all yourself?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.20,0:12:17.67,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Theron...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.60,0:12:20.07,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,Damn it!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.07,0:12:24.29,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,I was looking forward to this, since \NLiese got all fancy with the recipe.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.29,0:12:25.13,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,Theron...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.13,0:12:28.41,Main - Top,THERON,0,0,0,,You could've at least left me a bite.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.08,0:12:29.87,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,We were fighting together \Nuntil just moments ago, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.41,0:12:30.26,Main - Top,THERON,0,0,0,,You seriously ate all of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.13,0:12:32.81,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,What are you looking at?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.58,0:12:36.84,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,I, uh...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.63,0:12:40.82,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,What day of what month and year is it today?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.09,0:12:43.45,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,What're you on about?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.69,0:12:48.33,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,It's the 24th day of the fifth \Nmonth of the year 2823.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.75,0:12:50.92,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Really? You're sure?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.92,0:12:56.75,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,Yeah, it's definitely the 24th day \Nof the fifth month of the year 2823.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.75,0:12:59.21,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,Oh, right. Today's your birthday, yeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.51,0:13:01.48,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,Then I guess it's fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.48,0:13:04.59,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,We'll say that meal was your birthday present.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.59,0:13:06.34,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Kinda cheap, don't you think?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.59,0:13:08.75,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Besides, that wasn't yours to give.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.03,0:13:12.10,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,Man, I'm starving.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.10,0:13:14.45,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,I'm gonna go get something from Liese.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.31,0:13:21.45,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,If I kiss the ground and beg, \Nshe'll probably feed me a full meal.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.87,0:13:28.18,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,As usual, he'll do anything \Nto achieve his goals.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.42,0:13:33.29,Main - Italics,KYLE,0,0,0,,Now then, what should I do?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.73,0:13:36.58,Main - Italics,KYLE,0,0,0,,If I really have magically\N returned to the past...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.66,0:13:42.94,Main - Italics,KYLE,0,0,0,,Well... I'll have to ask {\i0}her{\i1} about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.54,0:14:13.49,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,Oh, Kyle. Rare to see you here.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.80,0:14:16.37,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,It's morning, Mom.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.63,0:14:18.75,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Were you up all night reading again?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.48,0:14:20.87,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,Morning already?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.87,0:14:24.13,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,I can never tell what time it is in here.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.35,0:14:27.26,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,To be honest, I have a magic question for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.85,0:14:30.14,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,Gosh, I don't know if I'll have an answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.42,0:14:33.61,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,You're an archmage. \NOne of only a handful in the country.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.09,0:14:37.16,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Not many people know more \Nabout magic than you do.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.64,0:14:39.11,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,I suppose not.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.68,0:14:45.53,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Listen, are there any spells \Nto return you to the past?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.53,0:14:46.71,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,There are.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.71,0:14:48.03,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,What? Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.60,0:14:53.66,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,They're not very well known, but there \Nare definitely spells that affect time.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.01,0:14:58.34,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,But we merely know they exist.\N Nobody can use them.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.34,0:15:00.90,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,It's a matter of the required magic power.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.90,0:15:02.17,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Magic power?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.44,0:15:07.31,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,Even if the greatest mage in history \Nused all their magic power,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.31,0:15:10.80,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,I doubt they could travel back \Neven a single second.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.07,0:15:13.68,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Then what about with\N the help of a magic item?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.01,0:15:16.90,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,I see. An interesting idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.90,0:15:20.40,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,You mean using a magic item \Nas a catalyst to store magic power?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.95,0:15:28.38,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,Even then, it would take someone over \Na millennium to store that much magic power.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.93,0:15:30.82,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,What if you used the Forbidden Rite?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.37,0:15:32.85,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,The Forbidden Rite...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.85,0:15:36.22,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,A sacrificial ritual to turn \Nlife force into magic power.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.35,0:15:38.83,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,Where did you learn about that?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.30,0:15:41.26,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,I just saw it in a book.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.58,0:15:42.90,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,I don't know much about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.30,0:15:44.30,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.17,0:15:47.55,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,Even with the Forbidden Rite,\N it'd be impossible.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.02,0:15:52.59,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,You'd need the lives of half \Nthe humanoids on the continent.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.13,0:15:57.45,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,In other words, it {\i0}is{\i1} possible \Nif you sacrifice half the land.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.85,0:16:00.14,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,On top of that,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.14,0:16:03.94,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,there's no catalyst capable of storing the\Nmagic power it'd take to go back in time.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.94,0:16:08.43,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,But if one... did exist...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.40,0:16:15.64,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,I think it'd be in this book.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.64,0:16:18.83,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,Ah, here we are.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.25,0:16:22.59,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,The legendary Divine Dragon's Heart \Nis just about your only option.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.29,0:16:28.94,Main - Italics,KYLE,0,0,0,,The ancient magic kingdom of Xarles
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.94,0:16:32.43,Main - Italics,KYLE,0,0,0,,prospered for a thousand years \Nthanks to the Divine Dragon's Heart
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.43,0:16:34.84,Main - Italics,KYLE,0,0,0,,and the tremendous magic power it contained.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.13,0:16:39.52,Main - Italics,KYLE,0,0,0,,But its power was eventually depleted,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.35,0:16:43.70,Main - Italics,KYLE,0,0,0,,leading to the kingdom's downfall.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.61,0:16:50.30,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,I'd bet the Divine Dragon's Heart could store\Nenough magic power to return to the past.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.62,0:16:55.49,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,But it's been missing\N for over a thousand years.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.86,0:16:58.84,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,Perhaps it's already fallen into demon hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.35,0:17:01.50,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.55,0:17:05.18,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,This is nice.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.18,0:17:05.86,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.91,0:17:11.65,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,It's been ages since we last talked this much.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.11,0:17:18.51,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,You quit your sword training \Nand you've been avoiding me lately...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.51,0:17:20.15,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Not on purpose!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.50,0:17:23.39,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,I, uh... I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.39,0:17:26.49,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,I swear! I've really missed you!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.62,0:17:31.89,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,But today, you seem more mature than usual.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.89,0:17:33.90,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,It's like you're here from the future.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.66,0:17:35.32,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.96,0:17:37.30,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,Just kidding.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.84,0:17:40.28,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,Gosh, I'm so hungry.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.28,0:17:43.16,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,Liese cooked for us again today, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.16,0:17:45.54,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Oh, uh... I ate it all.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.17,0:17:48.04,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.47,0:17:49.84,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Sorry! I couldn't help myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.84,0:17:51.21,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,It's fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.21,0:17:55.24,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,Oh, that reminds me!\N Today's your birthday, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.24,0:17:59.20,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,How like you to forget \Nyour own son's birthday.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.20,0:18:02.85,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,Then that meal can be your birthday present.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.19,0:18:07.82,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Why is everyone trying \Nto cheap out on my gift?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.72,0:18:21.97,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Returning to the past, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.09,0:18:25.92,Main - Italics,KYLE,0,0,0,,What did he want to do over?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.92,0:18:29.29,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,There you are.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.55,0:18:34.46,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Sorry about this morning!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.95,0:18:37.84,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,At least you feel bad about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.84,0:18:42.37,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,I only did it because I had \Na weird dream that upset me.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.37,0:18:43.60,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,I'm really sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.31,0:18:47.10,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,What kind of dream?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.28,0:18:54.28,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,Was it one about me dying?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.28,0:18:58.49,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Yeah, something like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.86,0:19:03.24,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,So that's why you were so distraught.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.59,0:19:05.79,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,Huh. I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.68,0:19:11.13,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,In that case, I forgive you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.13,0:19:13.13,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,Besides, today's your birthday.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.10,0:19:16.50,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,Happy birthday, Kyle!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.79,0:19:20.97,Main - Italics,KYLE,0,0,0,,Our town is close to demon territory.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.42,0:19:24.01,Main - Italics,KYLE,0,0,0,,It was the first to be attacked \Nin the Great Invasion.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.39,0:19:28.99,Main - Italics,KYLE,0,0,0,,They burned it to the ground, \Nleaving it a hellscape.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.92,0:19:31.36,Main - Italics,KYLE,0,0,0,,That's how I lost Liese.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.53,0:19:51.23,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,On that day, I swore I'd avenge her.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.70,0:19:54.96,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,Kyle. Kyle?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.65,0:19:57.17,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,What's wrong, Kyle?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.87,0:19:59.71,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,You're scaring me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.87,0:20:04.52,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,It's nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.40,0:20:08.22,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,Really? Then I guess it's fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.27,0:20:11.80,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,Three years from now, this peace will end.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.39,0:20:14.71,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,I'm the only one who knows.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.22,0:20:19.73,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,If I do nothing, I'll be forced \Nto witness the same thing over again.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.73,0:20:21.41,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,I'll lose them again—
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.07,0:20:27.22,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,My family, my home, my world, \Nand the people I love.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.08,0:20:30.13,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,I'll change it.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.87,0:20:32.00,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,My fate—
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.24,0:20:33.83,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,I'm going to change my fate!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.75,0:20:39.25,Main - Italics,KYLE,0,0,0,,I'll change my stupid fate \Nand the fate of the whole world!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.91,0:20:41.84,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,I swear I will!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.43,0:20:44.22,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,No matter what it takes!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:39.06,0:22:41.17,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,This is my advantage.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:41.78,0:22:46.15,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,I've logged all the future events I \Ncan remember in this notebook, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:46.81,0:22:48.05,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,Still...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:48.57,0:22:50.46,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,What should I be doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:50.98,0:22:53.43,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,I came here from four years in the future.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:53.43,0:22:57.65,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,The demons will launch an all-out \Nattack three years from now,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:58.06,0:23:02.31,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,but even if I tell people to prepare,\N nobody will believe me.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.58,0:23:09.12,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,I'll have to kill the mysterious \Ndemon king myself!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.99,0:23:13.17,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,That's not happening.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:13.57,0:23:16.12,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,Even if luck goes completely in my favor,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:16.12,0:23:18.45,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,I can't do this alone at my current strength.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:21.40,0:23:22.29,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,No...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:23.72,0:23:25.84,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,I should check first.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.01,0:23:40.25,Default,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\fnArial Black\fs12\shad0\blur1\bord1\3c&HB6A872&\pos(320,142.615)}Next Time
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.01,0:23:40.25,Default,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\an8\fnArial Black\fs18\shad0\blur1\3c&HB6A872&\pos(320,208.461)}The Hero's Conditions
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.96,0:23:39.36,Default,NA,0,0,0,,Next time: "The Hero's Conditions."
